/**
 * DIGIT shared Core DocTypes (owner decisions DEC-01 / DEC-02, 2026-11-11).
 *
 * Anything an app needs that the native catalog lacks — a DocType, a child table, a control record — is defined HERE, in
 * the shared Core, never inside an app plugin; apps point to it. The manifest below is always active (it is not an app
 * and cannot be disabled), overlaid by src/plugins/runtime.ts exactly like an app's DocTypes, and its routes use the
 * `core_` slug prefix so a Core DocType never collides with an app DocType of a similar name (e.g. HR's own
 * "DIGIT Approval Delegation" from the HR source).
 *
 * Moved from DIGIT Pro (names kept so stored records and every Pro screen keep working): Digit Approval Delegation,
 * Digit Pro Feature Control, Digit Pro Provider Setting. Pure data — no imports from the runtime.
 */
